# Environment / secrets.
#
# Added when visitor review submissions landed: .env now holds the Neon
# connection string — which carries the database owner's password in plain text
# and is not a scoped or rotatable token — plus the admin password, the session
# secret and the IP hash salt. Note .env was NOT ignored before this, because
# nothing secret existed yet. The .env.example negation has to come after the
# wildcard or git ignores the template too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

